    "function": "Involved in the biosynthesis of the maltose-1-phosphate (M1P) building block required for alpha-glucan production by the key enzyme GlgE. Catalyzes the formation of an alpha-1,4 linkage between glucose from ADP-glucose and glucose 1-phosphate (G1P) to yield maltose-1-phosphate (M1P). Also able to catalyze the elongation of the non-reducing ends of glycogen, maltodextrin and maltoheptaose using ADP-glucose as sugar donor, however the rate of the reaction appears to be too low to be physiologically relevant. GlgM is also able to use UDP-glucose as sugar donor with G1P, however, it is less effici",
